The attached image is relevant. The attached image displays box plots comparing anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 at varying doses (200, 50, and 12.5 µg/dose). The figure, identified as Fig. 9 in the 2015 JCR paper and Fig. 1 in the 2017 npj Vaccines paper, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances antibody responses to rPA, achieving titers comparable to or greater than those induced by AH, particularly at lower adjuvant doses.